#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:1
msgid "S3 Binary Cache Store"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:3
msgid "**Store URL format**: `s3://`_bucket-name_"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:5
msgid ""
"This store allows reading and writing a [binary cache](../../protocols/"
"binary-cache/index.md) stored in an AWS S3 (or S3-compatible service) "
"bucket. This store shares many idioms with the [HTTP Binary Cache Store]"
"(../../store/types/http-binary-cache-store.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:8
msgid ""
"For AWS S3, the binary cache URL for a bucket named `example-nix-cache` will "
"be exactly <s3://example-nix-cache>. For S3 compatible binary caches, "
"consult that cache's documentation."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:11
msgid "Anonymous reads to your S3-compatible binary cache"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:13
msgid ""
"If your binary cache is publicly accessible and does not require "
"authentication, it is simplest to use the \\[HTTP Binary Cache Store\\] "
"rather than S3 Binary Cache Store with <https://example-nix-"
"cache.s3.amazonaws.com> instead of <s3://example-nix-cache>."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:17
msgid ""
"Your bucket will need a [bucket policy](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/"
