#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:44
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:46
msgid ""
"Nix will use the [default credential provider chain](https://"
"docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-cpp/v1/developer-guide/credentials.html) for "
"authenticating requests to Amazon S3."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:50
msgid ""
"Note that this means Nix will read environment variables and files with "
"different idioms than with Nix's own settings, as implemented by the AWS "
"SDK. Consult the documentation linked above for further details."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:53
msgid "Authenticated reads to your S3 binary cache"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:55
msgid ""
"Your bucket will need a bucket policy allowing the desired users to perform "
"the `s3:GetObject`, `s3:GetBucketLocation`, and `s3:ListBucket` actions on "
"all objects in the bucket. The [anonymous policy given above](#anonymous-"
"reads-to-your-s3-compatible-binary-cache) can be updated to have a "
"restricted `Principal` to support this."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:58
msgid "Authenticated writes to your S3-compatible binary cache"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:60
msgid ""
