#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:87
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:89
msgid ""
"With bucket policies and authentication set up as described above, uploading "
"works via [`nix copy`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-copy.md) "
"(experimental)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:91
msgid "To upload with a specific credential profile for Amazon S3:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:93
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix copy nixpkgs.hello \\\n"
"  --to 's3://example-nix-cache?profile=cache-upload&region=eu-west-2'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:98
msgid "To upload to an S3-compatible binary cache:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:100
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix copy nixpkgs.hello --to \\\n"
"  's3://example-nix-cache?profile=cache-"
"upload&scheme=https&endpoint=minio.example.com'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:105
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:107
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-s3-binary-cache-store-addressing-style\">[`addressing-"
"style`](#store-s3-binary-cache-store-addressing-style)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:109
msgid ""
"The S3 addressing style to use. `auto` (default) uses virtual-hosted-style "
"for standard AWS endpoints and path-style for custom endpoints; bucket names "
"containing dots automatically fall back to path-style to avoid TLS "
"certificate errors. `path` forces path-style addressing (deprecated by AWS). "
"`virtual` forces virtual-hosted-style addressing (bucket names must not "
"contain dots)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:117
msgid "**Default:** `auto`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:119
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-s3-binary-cache-store-compression\">[`compression`](#store-"
"s3-binary-cache-store-compression)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:121
msgid ""
"NAR compression method. One of: `xz`, `bzip2`, `gzip`, `zstd`, `none`, `br`, "
"`compress`, `grzip`, `lrzip`, `lz4`, `lzip`, `lzma` or `lzop`. To use a "
"particular compression method Nix has to be built with a version of "
"libarchive that natively supports that compression algorithm."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:124
msgid "**Default:** `xz`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:126
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-s3-binary-cache-store-compression-level\">[`compression-"
"level`](#store-s3-binary-cache-store-compression-level)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:128
msgid ""
"The _preset level_ to be used when compressing NARs. The meaning and "
"accepted values depend on the compression method selected. `-1` specifies "
"that the default compression level should be used."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:132
msgid "**Default:** `-1`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:134
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-s3-binary-cache-store-endpoint\">[`endpoint`](#store-s3-"
"binary-cache-store-endpoint)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:136
msgid ""
"The S3 endpoint to use. When empty (default), uses AWS S3 with region-"
"specific endpoints. For S3-compatible services such as MinIO, set this to "
"your service's endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:140
#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:285
msgid "**Default:** _empty_"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:142
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-s3-binary-cache-store-index-debug-info\">[`index-debug-"
"info`](#store-s3-binary-cache-store-index-debug-info)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:144
msgid ""
"Whether to index DWARF debug info files by build ID. This allows [`dwarffs`]"
"(https://github.com/edolstra/dwarffs) to fetch debug info on demand"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:147
#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:194
#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:208
#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:342
#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:348
#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:354
msgid "**Default:** `false`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:149
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-s3-binary-cache-store-local-nar-cache\">[`local-nar-cache`]"
"(#store-s3-binary-cache-store-local-nar-cache)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:151
msgid ""
"Path to a local cache of NARs fetched from this binary cache, used by "
"commands such as `nix store cat`."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:153
#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:161
#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:167
#: source/store/types/s3-binary-cache-store.md:200
